add('Assign Cookies', '''    public static int solve(int[] greed,int[] sizes){ int[] g=greed.clone(),s=sizes.clone(); Arrays.sort(g); Arrays.sort(s); int i=0; for(int x:s) if(i<g.length && x>=g[i]) i++; return i; }''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{1,2,3},new int[]{1,1}));','1',
    'Each child needs one cookie of at least its greed value; each cookie serves at most one child. Maximize satisfied children.', 'Sort both lists. Give the smallest sufficient cookie to the least greedy remaining child. An exchange replacing a larger cookie with this one cannot hurt the child and preserves larger cookies for others.', 'O(n log n+m log m) time; O(n+m) copy space.', 'Cookie 1 satisfies greed 1; second cookie 1 cannot satisfy greed 2.', 'Arrays are copied; zero children/cookies is valid. Values are assumed nonnegative.')
add('Lemonade Change', '''    public static boolean solve(int[] bills){ int five=0,ten=0; for(int b:bills){ if(b==5) five++; else if(b==10){ if(five==0) return false; five--; ten++; } else if(b==20){ if(ten>0&&five>0){ ten--; five--; } else if(five>=3) five-=3; else return false; } else throw new IllegalArgumentException(); } return true; }''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{5,5,5,10,20}));','true',
    'A drink costs 5. Customers pay 5,10,20 in order; start with no cash and return whether every change can be made.', 'For a 20 bill prefer 10+5 over 5+5+5 because fives are the only way to change a future 10. Twenties never help make change.', 'O(n) time; O(1) space.', 'Three fives -> one ten consumes a five -> twenty uses ten+five.', 'Future bills cannot pay current change; do not aggregate the whole queue first.')
add('Fractional Knapsack', '''    public static double solve(int[][] items,int capacity){ if(capacity<0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(); int[][] a=new int[items.length][]; for(int i=0;i<a.length;i++){ a[i]=items[i].clone(); if(a[i][0]<0||a[i][1]<=0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(); } Arrays.sort(a,(x,y)->Double.compare((double)y[0]/y[1],(double)x[0]/x[1])); double value=0; int remaining=capacity; for(int[] item:a){ int take=Math.min(remaining,item[1]); value+=(double)item[0]*take/item[1]; remaining-=take; if(remaining==0) break; } return value; }''','System.out.println(solve(new int[][]{{60,10},{100,20},{120,30}},50));','240.0',
    'Items are [value,positive weight], nonnegative values. Fractions are allowed; maximize value within integer capacity.', 'Sort by value per weight. An exchange of equal weight from a lower-density portion to a higher-density portion never decreases value, so consume densities in descending order.', 'O(n log n) time; O(n) copy space.', 'Take 10 weight for 60, 20 for 100, then 20/30 of 120 for 80; total 240.', 'This greedy proof relies on divisible items. The 0/1 version requires a different algorithm.')
add('Jump Game - I', '''    public static boolean solve(int[] a){ long far=0; for(int i=0;i<a.length;i++){ if(i>far) return false; if(a[i]<0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(); far=Math.max(far,(long)i+a[i]); } return a.length>0; }''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{2,3,1,1,4}));','true',
    'Nonnegative jump lengths allow any jump up to a[i]; determine whether last index is reachable from zero. Empty input is false.', 'All indices up to far are reachable. If next i lies outside far there is a gap no prior jump crosses; otherwise update the frontier.', 'O(n) time; O(1) space.', 'At 0 frontier 2; at 1 frontier 4, reaching the last index.', 'Use long for i+a[i]. A singleton is reachable without a jump.')
add('Jump Game II', '''    public static int solve(int[] a){ if(a.length==0) return -1; long end=0,far=0; int jumps=0; for(int i=0;i<a.length-1;i++){ if(a[i]<0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(); if(i>far) return -1; far=Math.max(far,(long)i+a[i]); if(i==end){ if(far==end) return -1; jumps++; end=far; if(end>=a.length-1) return jumps; } } return 0; }''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{2,3,1,1,4}));','2',
    'Return the minimum jumps to the last index or -1 if unreachable, with nonnegative max jump lengths.', 'Process reachable indices in BFS-like layers. end is the boundary reachable with current jumps; far is the next layer frontier. Cross each layer boundary once.', 'O(n) time; O(1) space.', 'First layer from index 0 reaches 2; scanning indices 1,2 extends next frontier to 4, requiring two jumps.', 'Do not increment jumps for each frontier increase. Zero-length progress at a layer boundary means unreachable.')
add('Shortest Job First', '''    public static double solve(int[] bursts){ if(bursts.length==0) return 0; int[] a=bursts.clone(); Arrays.sort(a); long elapsed=0,total=0; for(int x:a){ if(x<0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(); total+=elapsed; elapsed+=x; } return (double)total/a.length; }''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{3,1,2}));','1.3333333333333333',
    'All jobs arrive at time zero; nonpreemptive jobs have nonnegative durations. Return average waiting time.', 'Run shortest duration first. Swapping a longer-then-shorter adjacent pair reduces the waiting contributed to the shorter job without changing later completion time.', 'O(n log n) time; O(n) copy space.', 'Sorted 1,2,3 gives waits 0,1,3; average 4/3.', 'Different arrival times require scheduling with a priority queue; this contract has simultaneous arrivals.')
add('Job sequencing Problem', '''    public static long[] solve(int[][] jobs){ int[][] a=jobs.clone(); Arrays.sort(a,(x,y)->Integer.compare(y[1],x[1])); int max=0; for(int[] j:a) max=Math.max(max,j[0]); int[] slot=new int[Math.min(max,a.length)+1]; Arrays.fill(slot,-1); long profit=0,count=0; for(int[] j:a){ if(j[1]<=0) continue; for(int t=Math.min(j[0],slot.length-1);t>=1;t--) if(slot[t]==-1){ slot[t]=1; count++; profit+=j[1]; break; } } return new long[]{count,profit}; }''','System.out.println(Arrays.toString(solve(new int[][]{{2,100},{1,19},{2,27},{1,25},{3,15}})));','[3, 142]',
    'Each job takes one time unit and is [deadline,profit]. Maximize profit by completing before deadlines; return [jobs done,total profit]. Nonpositive-profit jobs may be skipped.', 'Consider profit descending and schedule at the latest free slot before its deadline. This keeps earlier slots available for tighter deadlines. Unit-duration deadline scheduling admits this greedy exchange.', 'O(n log n+n*min(n,maxDeadline)) time; O(min(n,maxDeadline)) slot space plus sorted copy.', 'Schedule profit 100 at slot 2, profit 27 at slot 1, profit 15 at slot 3; total 142.', 'The algorithm does not apply to variable-duration jobs. Deadlines <=0 are unschedulable.', 'A disjoint-set latest-free-slot structure improves scheduling to near-linear after sorting.')
interval_code = '''    public static int[][] sorted(int[][] intervals){ int[][] a=new int[intervals.length][]; for(int i=0;i<a.length;i++){ a[i]=intervals[i].clone(); if(a[i][0]>a[i][1]) throw new IllegalArgumentException(); } return a; }'''
add('N meetings in one room',interval_code+'''\n    public static int solve(int[][] input){ int[][] a=sorted(input); Arrays.sort(a,(x,y)->Integer.compare(x[1],y[1])); long end=Long.MIN_VALUE; int count=0; for(int[] x:a) if(x[0]>end){ count++; end=x[1]; } return count; }''','System.out.println(solve(new int[][]{{1,2},{3,4},{0,6},{5,7},{8,9},{5,9}}));','4',
    'Maximize nonoverlapping meetings [start,end]. This variant requires the next start STRICTLY after the previous end.', 'Always choose the earliest finishing compatible meeting. Replacing an optimal first choice with this earlier finisher leaves at least as much time for remaining meetings.', 'O(n log n) time; O(n) copy space.', 'Choose [1,2],[3,4],[5,7],[8,9].', 'Some judges allow touching endpoints; change > to >= for that contract. Equal finish times are harmless to count.')
add('Non-overlapping Intervals',interval_code+'''\n    public static int solve(int[][] input){ int[][] a=sorted(input); Arrays.sort(a,(x,y)->Integer.compare(x[1],y[1])); long end=Long.MIN_VALUE; int kept=0; for(int[] x:a) if(x[0]>=end){ kept++; end=x[1]; } return a.length-kept; }''','System.out.println(solve(new int[][]{{1,2},{2,3},{3,4},{1,3}}));','1',
    'Return minimum intervals to remove so remaining intervals do not overlap; touching endpoints are allowed.', 'Maximize kept intervals with earliest finishing compatible choices, then subtract from total. The earliest-finish exchange argument proves the kept count is optimal.', 'O(n log n) time; O(n) copy space.', 'Keep [1,2],[2,3],[3,4], removing [1,3].', 'This contract uses >= unlike strict meeting scheduling.')
merge_intervals = interval_code+'''\n    public static int[][] solve(int[][] input){ int[][] a=sorted(input); Arrays.sort(a,(x,y)->Integer.compare(x[0],y[0])); List<int[]> out=new ArrayList<>(); for(int[] x:a){ if(out.isEmpty()||out.get(out.size()-1)[1]<x[0]) out.add(x.clone()); else { int[] last=out.get(out.size()-1); last[1]=Math.max(last[1],x[1]); } } return out.toArray(new int[out.size()][]); }'''
add('Merge Intervals',merge_intervals,'System.out.println(Arrays.deepToString(solve(new int[][]{{1,3},{2,6},{8,10},{15,18}})));','[[1, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]',
    'Merge overlapping closed intervals; touching endpoints merge. Return a new array.', 'Sort by start. A new interval either extends the last merged block or starts a new disjoint block. Future starts cannot overlap earlier blocks without also reaching the last.', 'O(n log n) time; O(n) space.', '[1,3] and [2,6] combine to [1,6]; subsequent starts 8 and 15 create new blocks.', 'Use max on end: a contained interval must not shrink a block. Inputs are copied.')
add('Insert Interval',merge_intervals.replace('solve(int[][] input)','merge(int[][] input)')+'''\n    public static int[][] solve(int[][] a,int[] x){ int[][] all=Arrays.copyOf(a,a.length+1); all[a.length]=x; return merge(all); }''','System.out.println(Arrays.deepToString(solve(new int[][]{{1,3},{6,9}},new int[]{2,5})));','[[1, 5], [6, 9]]',
    'Insert a closed interval and merge overlaps. This implementation accepts unsorted input too.', 'Append the new interval and reuse general sort-and-merge. Correctness follows from the merge invariant.', 'O(n log n) time; O(n) space.', 'Sort [1,3],[2,5],[6,9], merging the first two.', 'When original input is already sorted and disjoint, a three-phase scan gives O(n) time: copy before, merge overlaps, copy after.')
add('Minimum number of platforms required for a railway', '''    public static int solve(int[] arrival,int[] departure){ if(arrival.length!=departure.length) throw new IllegalArgumentException(); int[] a=arrival.clone(),d=departure.clone(); Arrays.sort(a); Arrays.sort(d); int i=0,j=0,active=0,best=0; while(i<a.length){ if(j==d.length || a[i]<=d[j]){ active++; best=Math.max(best,active); i++; } else { active--; j++; } } return best; }''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{900,940,950,1100,1500,1800},new int[]{910,1200,1120,1130,1900,2000}));','3',
    'Each train has arrival<=departure on the same day. Count minimum simultaneous platforms; an arrival exactly at a departure needs another platform.', 'Sort event times independently and sweep. An arrival increases active platforms; a departure frees one. Maximum concurrent active trains is both necessary and sufficient.', 'O(n log n) time; O(n) copies.', 'At 1100 the trains arriving 940,950,1100 overlap until 1120, requiring three.', 'Overnight trains need a normalized day-aware timeline. Change <= to < if touching times may reuse a platform.')
add('Valid Paranthesis Checker', '''    public static boolean solve(String s){ int low=0,high=0; for(char c:s.toCharArray()){ if(c=='('){ low++; high++; } else if(c==')'){ low--; high--; } else if(c=='*'){ low--; high++; } else throw new IllegalArgumentException(); if(high<0) return false; low=Math.max(low,0); } return low==0; }''','System.out.println(solve("(*))"));','true',
    'For (,),* where * may be (,),or empty, decide if some replacement gives balanced parentheses.', 'Track a RANGE of possible open counts. * expands low down/high up; clamp low to zero because negative opens are invalid. If high becomes negative, every interpretation fails. At the end zero must be in the range.', 'O(n) time; O(1) space.', '(*)): ranges [1,1] -> [0,2] -> [0,1] -> [0,0].', 'This is the wildcard-parentheses variant; ordinary bracket matching uses a stack.', 'Trying all three meanings of every star is O(3^stars). DP memoizes index/open states.')
add('Candy', '''    public static long solve(int[] a){ if(a.length==0) return 0; int[] candy=new int[a.length]; Arrays.fill(candy,1); for(int i=1;i<a.length;i++) if(a[i]>a[i-1]) candy[i]=candy[i-1]+1; for(int i=a.length-2;i>=0;i--) if(a[i]>a[i+1]) candy[i]=Math.max(candy[i],candy[i+1]+1); long sum=0; for(int x:candy) sum+=x; return sum; }''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{1,0,2}));','5',
    'Every child receives at least one candy; higher rating than either neighbor needs strictly more candy. Minimize total.', 'Left-to-right enforces the left-neighbor constraint minimally. Right-to-left enforces the right constraint using max to preserve the left one. Each assigned count is the minimum satisfying both slopes.', 'O(n) time; O(n) space.', '[1,0,2] left pass [1,1,2], right pass [2,1,2], sum 5.', 'Equal ratings impose no ordering requirement. Total needs long for long slopes.', 'A slope-based one-pass method uses O(1) space but must carefully subtract the shared peak when joining ascent and descent.')
